    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0104" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.002/1–2849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-28T15:00:00+08:00">January 28, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 29—6:33 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>260. Premier<anchor n="84" xml:id="d113-f1"/> and Foreign Minister have already
                    left Nanking probably en route Canton. Despite statement by Vice Foreign <pb
                        facs="0105" n="95" xml:id="pg95"/> Minister that they have gone to Shanghai
                    for special purpose and are returning Nanking, their houses are both entirely
                    closed and empty.</p>
                <p>Repeated Shanghai 116, Canton 13.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d113-f1" n="84" xml:id="d113-f1-content">
